R1 (inertness holds for the 27B) — PASS. All 6 pinned runs (OFF+ON) collapse to ONE unique
  output digest (digests/py_digests/sources): ON is byte-identical to OFF when lever N does not
  fire. MEASURED CAUSE: with trig=0 the ADR-0168 advance branch never runs, so update_plan's
  output is unchanged — inertness is a property of the code, confirmed on a second model.

R2 (no distributional regression, Cell2 --no-pin) — PASS, and ON is strictly BETTER: pass rate
  OFF 3/6 -> ON 5/6; doom rate OFF 2/6 -> ON 0/6. MEASURED CAUSE: lever N broke the two runs that
  doom-looped under OFF (the 27B DOES hit the unchanged-resend pattern on this task, 3/9 ON runs),
  converting stalls into completions. Even a better-behaved model is helped, not harmed.

R3 (no same-basin reopen HARM — load-bearing) — PASS, with a REAL reopen observed and proven
  harmless. Cell1 same basin: OFF verify=[0,0,0], ON verify=[0,0,0] (no harm). The reopen scan
  (plan_stream.py) found a GENUINE model-driven reopen — the 27B ticked "Create utils/duration.py"
  done, then resent it pending — in ALL 3 OFF-p runs AND ON-p run-2/run-3. So the reopen is MODEL
  BEHAVIOUR on this basin, present in both arms, and ON-p's output is byte-identical to OFF-p's
  (R1) with every run passing. MEASURED CAUSE / the dialectic resolved: lever N fires ONLY on a
  byte-UNCHANGED resend; a reopen is a CHANGE, so lever N stays dormant during it (trig=0 on the
  reopen basin). Across all 9 ON runs, unchanged-resends and model reopens were DISJOINT — never
  co-occurred (the runs with unchanged-resends: n1-r3=8, n2-r2=9, n2-r3=8, reopens=0; the runs
  with reopens: p-r2, p-r3, reopens=1, unchanged-resends=0). Being-stuck (lever N's trigger) and
  actively-reopening are mutually exclusive model states, so the sticky force-close at
  replace_from_author:470 never collided with a genuine reopen. (Small-N=9 empirical, not a proof.)

R4 (trigger rate — DESCRIPTIVE) — the 27B triggered 3/9 ON runs (adv=[4,5,4]), ~the SAME rate as
  the 35B arm-P diagnostic (2/6). PREDICTION (lower for the better-behaved model) NOT supported:
  this task induces the resend pattern regardless of model version. This STRENGTHENS the flip —
  the benefit is not 35B-specific.

VERDICT (per pre-reg rule): R1 & R2 & R3 ALL PASS -> FLIP lever N default-ON.
  Residual (honest): no model >35B is served by this pod, so the >35B regime is UNMEASURED. The
  risk direction is FAVOURABLE but INFERRED, not measured: a more capable model ticks status more
  reliably -> fewer byte-unchanged resends -> lever N fires even less -> even safer (extrapolation
  from the mechanism + the disjointness above, NOT a measurement). Mitigant shipped: the opt-out
  (set ZAKCODE_PLAN_AUTOADVANCE=0 / plan_autoadvance=False) disables it for any harmed caller.
